## Session 45 — VIP Workflow Settings surface, remote transport

183 tool calls / 63 min. **This is the counterweight to session 44**: same repo, same Figma file, same libraries — but built with first-class tools instead of a `run_script` monoculture.

| | S44 | S45 |
|---|---|---|
| `run_script` share of Figmagent calls | 69% | **28%** |
| `write`/`edit`/`lint`/`grep` calls | **0** | **43** |
| Figmagent error rate | 9.8% | **5.3%** |
| Nodes created / edited | — | 349 / 272 |

That drop is strong evidence session 44's monoculture was driven by capability gaps, not agent preference — the residual 32 scripts map almost one-to-one onto tracked issues.

**The headline finding is worse, though.** `[BUG-016]` (remote `screenshot` → `-32602 invalid_union`) recurred for the 7th time, and the defection to the official Figma MCP has crossed from behavior into *state*: call #2 of the session read a memory file written at the end of session 44 that says verbatim *"Figmagent's `screenshot` tool is broken here — use `mcp__plugin_figma_figma__get_screenshot` and `curl` the returned URL instead."* The agent tried once, failed, and ran the competitor for 41 minutes — 35 calls to accomplish 11 visual checks (24 net waste, ~7 min). Three of those official-MCP calls returned unusable 1×1 PNGs, so the fallback isn't even reliable. **Landing the code fix is no longer sufficient — that memory file has to be corrected in the same pass.**

Four new bugs, all pinned to source:
- `[BUG-024]` `set_focus` on remote prints `Focused on node "undefined" (ID: undefined)` — `remote/transport.ts:30–34` returns a `note` that `tools/scan.ts:144–152` discards.
- `[BUG-025]` `create.js:161` calls `importComponentByKeyAsync` bare, no `fail(message, fix)` — the only branch in that block without one. Rejected a variant key the agent had harvested 13 min earlier.
- `[BUG-026]` `script.ts:147–155` returns the `mode:"read"` rejection without `isError: true` — a script that never ran reads as success.
- `[TOOL-030]` no variant-property filter on `get_component_variants`, and no way to read a published component's nested property API without instantiating it in a scratch frame (~9 `run_script` calls).

Plus `[AGENT-026]`: script #164 set nine properties `edit` already exposes — including `clipsContent`, the already-shipped half of `[TOOL-027]`.

Recurrences logged: `BUG-014` (7th), `TOOL-021` (3rd), `TOOL-026` (3rd), `TOOL-025` (2nd). No new auto-fix plans — none of the five match the Phase 6 allowlist.
