## The headline: BUG-016's fix is half-verified, half-falsified

This was the first live remote session after commit `0af2c9a` landed. Both things it was supposed to do, it did:

- **Zero `-32602 invalid_union` protocol crashes** across 11 export failures — every one arrived as readable text with `is_error: true`.
- **Zero calls to the official Figma MCP**, under heavier provocation than either prior session (11 failures vs 3 in session 44, 1 in session 45). Sessions 44 and 45 defected and lost 62 and 24 calls. This agent diagnosed the gap in-line, verified by sub-frame screenshots plus `run_script` measurement, and shipped. Correcting the downstream memory file alongside the code is what made that hold.

But the export failure itself is untouched, and **the new error message misdiagnoses it**. `screenshot` failed 11/25 (44%), all blaming the "~4MB return cap". Four proofs that's wrong:

1. The cap's own error (`document.js:655`, naming the actual char count) never appears — the observed text is the `export.ts` fallback guard, which fires on absent `imageData` and *guesses*.
2. `2377:38` is **220×132 px** and failed at `scale: 2`. `2372:2` is 248×327 at `scale: 1`.
3. All three recommended remedies were tried and all failed — lower `scale`, `format: "SVG"`, smaller child node.
4. `screenshot(2372:24, scale:1)` **succeeded at 22:46:30 and failed at 22:53:00**. Size can't explain a result that flips in seven minutes.

Batch mode also drops healthy nodes with sick ones: a 3-node batch returned `Exported 0 node(s): none` with no `Errors:` block, then the same node exported cleanly alone five seconds later.

## New finding: the same hole is open in `read`

One `read` returned a well-formed, empty, **`is_error: false`** FSGN document for a node that call #5 had just listed as present. The `meta` block was missing `nodeId`/`name`/`type` — which `tools/document.ts:87–90` copies unconditionally — proving the handler got an empty object and serialized it as success. `nodeCount: 0` is impossible from `getNodeTree`, which increments before any filter. Same silent-empty-result condition as BUG-016, but strictly worse: screenshot at least says something failed, `read` reports success. The agent accepted `nodes: []` and never inspected that subtree.

Filed as **[BUG-027]** (P0) with the fix: mirror `export.ts`'s `hasImageData` guard, and audit the other remote result-builders — `0af2c9a` closed this for one file and left it open everywhere else. Also filed **[BUG-028]** (`read` emits absolute coords, `edit` writes parent-local, neither says so — cost 2 recovery scripts and a 2656px misplacement) and **[AGENT-027]** (frame resize rescales SCALE-constrained children). `[TOOL-026]` logged its 4th consecutive recurrence.

BUG-016 gets a v4 fix proposal: return `payloadChars` from `exportSingleNode` so the guard can say "the plugin rendered 41,204 chars but the transport returned none" instead of asserting a cap that never fired — and suppress the scale/SVG remedies when the payload is nowhere near the limit.

No fix plans generated — none of the new issues match the Phase 6 auto-fix allowlist. The four changed/added files are written but unstaged.
