Built 26 `pattern/*` preview cards across 5 sections on a 1792×14718 board from real published Gutenberg/WPDS library instances — entirely through `run_script` (28 calls, 126,546 chars; zero `write`/`edit`/`lint`).

**Three findings:**

**[BUG-016], 11th recurrence — the decisive control.** Two batch `screenshot` calls returned `Exported 0 node(s): none`, and every constituent node then exported cleanly one-by-one **at a larger scale** seconds later (`scale: 0.6` batch fails → members at 0.8 succeed). Holding the nodes fixed kills any size-based explanation. Two more single-path falsifications: a **552×273** frame failed at `scale: 0.8` (new smallest-render record), and the board failed at **`scale: 0.06`**. All consistent with the pinned v5 root cause at `remote/client.ts:110-114` and nothing else. The v3 guards held again — zero protocol crashes, and **zero official-MCP defection in a project with no corrected memory file**, now 4 sessions across 3 repos.

**[AGENT-028] — `resize()` on an auto-layout primary axis silently flips it to `FIXED`.** A helper did `primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'` then `resize(w, 1)`, pinning **17 frames at height 1**. It read as a *rendering* fault (null render bounds, 149-byte PNGs), so the agent burned 10 calls and ~8 minutes on reflow/rasterization/viewport hypotheses before isolating it. Sibling to [AGENT-027] — same call, second silent side effect.

**[BUG-031] — the remote VM throws `Node not found` for instance-descendant IDs it just returned.** `.children`/`findAll()` hand out `I<a>;<b>;<c>` IDs that the next property read refuses to resolve. Three scripts died atomically, discarding **35,304 chars** of authored script.

Filed **AGENT-028**, **BUG-031**, **TOOL-033** (`run_script` emits no post-write assertions, and no assertion covers height collapse — this consolidates a caveat repeated in five existing entries and finally costs it). Recurrences logged: TOOL-021 (5th), AGENT-025 (4th), TOOL-031 (3rd).

