## Two new confirmed bugs, both traced to source

**[BUG-041] `fig.loadFont` reports success for a font it never loaded.** `loadFontWithFallback` (`helpers.js`) catches `loadFontAsync`'s throw, silently substitutes Inter, and returns `{family: "Inter"}` as success — and `stdlib.js:25` exposes it directly as `fig.loadFont`. Script #20 awaited it twice, both resolved, then died 30 lines later on `set_fontName`, discarding a ~120-line atomic build. This is the half of [BUG-033]'s proposed fix that *cannot fire*: the throw is swallowed before any caller sees it. The fallback is correct for internal callers — the fix belongs at the stdlib boundary.

