## What the session was

64 minutes in `~/Github/storybook` on the "Archer" file (remote transport): scope all 596 Figma variables, create 8 `ui/*` text styles and apply them across 15 component pages, then give the repo's `Checkbox` a label. 134 tool calls, 2 errors, two clean commits.

## Headline finding

**`run_script` hit 80% of Figma calls (28 of 35) and 100% of write ops — both records.** But this is the first session that separates the two causes of [AGENT-025] in one transcript:

- **Discovery failure** — `create_styles`/`update_styles` were never ToolSearched, so the text-style phase never had them as candidates. Both ToolSearch calls landed in the first 8 minutes; the phase that needed different tools started at 03:41 and ran 43 more minutes.
- **Preference failure** — `update_variables` and `create_variables` *were* in context at 03:22 and still lost to a script. The incentive is visible: a 596-variable scope change is ~2.5KB as a run-length-encoded script and ~48KB as a first-class call.

Fixing either alone leaves the other.

## The best of the six new entries

**[TOOL-050]** — the agent spent 5 scripts empirically rediscovering a recipe `create_styles` already implements. `styles.js:903-957` runs create → set font → metrics → bind variables *last*, which is exactly the order the session derived at #8. Two description defects hide it: the font-loading line reads as "name the real family" (which throws on remote), and the bindable-fields list omits `fontWeight` even though `bindVariablesToStyle` passes it straight through — so `fontWeight` binding **works on this surface today**, unlike on `edit`. That sharpens [TOOL-037]: the `create_styles` half needs only a doc change, `edit`/`fig.bindVariable` still need the three-part code fix.

Also new: [TOOL-051] (`grep` has no absence criterion — 4 scripts asking "what's still unstyled"), [AGENT-036], [TOOL-052], [TOOL-053], [TOOL-054].

## Two corrections worth flagging

- I initially wrote in the tracker header that session 62 had no overlap with sessions 60/61. The timing data contradicts that — its window **fully contains both**. I corrected the header and added a Concurrency Exposure section. Only one write (the 596-variable re-scope at 03:30:44Z) lands inside their active write windows; the dangerous one, the document-wide park-and-swap that touches the very page session 61 had just built, missed it by 19 minutes. No interference is visible in the outcome.
- [TOOL-050]'s central claim is a code-path reading plus the session's step-by-step empirical proof of each element — not an executed end-to-end `create_styles` call. I marked that caveat on the entry, along with one latent fragility (`bindVariablesToStyle` iterates `Object.keys` with no ordering guarantee).

Corroborations recorded on [BUG-037] (3-for-3 with the park, clean failure without it), [BUG-033] (6th, new call site `loadFontOrFail`), [TOOL-029] (28/28 `stdlib: false`), [TOOL-031], and the [BUG-014] onboarding half (5th occurrence — at this point the proposed docs line should just ship).
